# The checks of the C++ package: the C++ Core Guidelines, the bug-prone
# patterns, the CERT rules, the static analyser, and the concurrent,
# miscellaneous, modern, fast, portable, and readable forms, every finding an
# error. Diplomat's generated headers are left out. A trailing return type is
# not the layer's style, and a switch over an enumeration lists every
# enumerator without a default, so that the compiler's -Wswitch refuses one
# that a new enumerator is missing from. The names follow the package's rule:
# PascalCase for types and template parameters, camelCase for functions,
# methods, variables, parameters, and members (camelBack admits no
# underscore, so no name carries an affix), UPPER_CASE for constants, enum
# values, and macros, and lowercase namespaces. Short names are the words
# and the initialism the repository admits: to and id. Diplomat's headers
# include one another in cycles, which their include guards resolve, and its
# asynchronous calls move a callback and then read its type from what is
# left, which the analyser's moved-from check reports through every call of
# the layer; bugprone-use-after-move checks the layer's own moves. A
# parameter taken by value is const in its declaration too, so that the
# declaration reads as the definition does. Every function a header defines
# writes inline, even where the language implies it, so readability's check of
# a redundant inline is off. The groups enable the checks that keep the
# qualifiers: misc-const-correctness, which also asks for a pointer that is
# never reseated to be const itself (T *const),
# readability-make-member-function-const, modernize-use-nodiscard,
# misc-explicit-constructor, the performance-noexcept checks, and
# bugprone-exception-escape, which reads throw expressions and so finds none
# in a lint built without exceptions, as the tests and the ports are. No check
# finds a function that could be noexcept, a parameter taken by value that
# could be const, or a local of a template that could be const; those are kept
# by reading.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-switch-missing-default-case,
  -clang-analyzer-cplusplus.Move,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-avoid-const-params-in-decls,
  -readability-redundant-inline-specifier
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(.*/)?include/eranos(/.*)?\.hpp$'
CheckOptions:
  misc-const-correctness.TransformPointersAsValues: true
  misc-const-correctness.WarnPointersAsValues: true
  misc-header-include-cycle.IgnoredFilesList: 'Eranos[A-Za-z]*\.(d\.)?h(pp)?'
  misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes.IgnoreClassesWithAllMemberVariablesBeingPublic: true
  readability-identifier-length.IgnoredParameterNames: '^(id|to)$'
  readability-identifier-length.IgnoredVariableNames: '^(id|to)$'
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.UnionCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TemplateParameterCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.MemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.LocalConstantCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantParameterCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.ScopedEnumConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionCase: UPPER_CASE
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase: lower_case
